CORE
main.cpp
--cpp20 --object-bits 11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ empty-pack base keeps sibling derived-to-base: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
N5008 [temp.variadic]/7: an empty pack expansion produces an empty list, so a
base-specifier argument `Empty<_Tail...>` with empty `_Tail` collapses to
`Empty<>` and the base is kept.

Regression (models libstdc++ tuple's _Tuple_impl / _Head_base layout):
instantiating a variadic class that derives from both an empty-pack base
(`Empty<_Tail...>`) and a sibling base (`Head_base`) left the empty pack
expansion unsubstituted; resolving that malformed base threw and discarded the
entire base list, so the sibling base was lost and a derived-to-base argument
conversion (`Impl& -> Head_base&`) failed -- the call was dropped and the
function returned a nondet reference.  Fixed by dropping empty pack expansions
from base-specifier argument lists during instantiation.  Assertion 2 (a wrong
value) FAILs, proving non-vacuity.
